  "follow_up_561": {
    "cause": "InstrumentSplits and TradeQuotePendingSplits built correction roots for every investment operation in the book (top-down recursive CTE), so cost grew with investment history; under QPSG InstrumentSplits also full-scanned investment_split_facts",
    "fix": [
      "correctionRootsOf seeds the walk with the operations a read needs and climbs correction_of_operation_id by primary key (CROSS JOIN keeps seeds first)",
      "InstrumentSplits selects effective splits in range once (materialized CTE) as both seed and result; superseded versions are no longer starting points, so each chain is walked once rather than once per version, but the walk from an effective split still visits its superseded predecessors as ancestors; the instrument list is bound once",
      "TradeQuotePendingSplits matches trade-implied observations to same-day effective splits once, reading observations once and seeking splits by index (CROSS JOIN), and seeds from the matches",
      "migration 0012 adds investment_split_facts_lookup_idx (book_id, commodity_id, effective_on)"
    ],
    "probe": "backend/internal/app/split_query_cost_test.go: SPLIT_QUERY_COST=1, SPLIT_QUERY_OPS (buys), SPLIT_QUERY_SPLITS (alternating 2:1/1:2), SPLIT_QUERY_REPLACEMENTS (replacements of the last split); one holding, two instrument ids",
    "keys": "read|operations|build",
    "tests": [
      "TestCorrectionRootsOfMatchesReplayOrderRoots",
      "TestTradeQuoteBeforeALaterDaySplitIsNotPending",
